      "Four-axis score — peptide 0/5; AI-agent infrastructure 5/5 (companion RNA-seq + CUT&Tag is the canonical cross-omics input for AI-DD target nomination, enabling peak-to-gene linkage scoring); longevity 2/5 (HCC is age-associated but the lane is clinical not longevity); cost 4/5 (2 datasets, older pdat adds modest QC burden, raw files enable immediate re-analysis). The signal is actionable from the BB multiomics + AI-DD service stack as an EZH2i + ferroptosis-inducer combination brief.",
      "Why it matters for BB + action — Ingest both datasets, run H3K27me3-peak-to-gene linkage scoring at EZH2-target-genes (intersect CUT&Tag peaks with RNA-seq DEGs at FDR<0.05, log2FC>1), stratify responders by SLC7A11/xCT and GPX4 baseline expression, integrate with TCGA-LIHC EZH2-high vs EZH2-low survival cohorts and DepMap CRISPR co-dependencies, and package as a candidate list of EZH2i + ferroptosis-inducer combinations for HCC. The first deliverable should be a 3-page EZH2-ferroptosis cross-target prioritization brief with explicit combination-strategy scoring (synergy score, safety margin, IND-stage prioritization), not a compound recommendation. The 2 older companion datasets (pdat 2024/10/25) should be cross-validated against newer 2025-2026 HCC ferroptosis atlases to confirm signal persistence before client delivery.",
      "Signal 3 — Longevity + Cellular Senescence + Reproductive Aging + Women's Health / Single-Cell Transcriptomics Reveals Ovarian Aging and Senescent Cell Accumulation underlying the Estropausal Transition in Mice: GSE267729 (watcher score 4, n=18, Mus musculus, single-cell RNA-seq 'Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing', pdat 2026/07/01 = 63 days ago, raw files yes, watcher query 'sarcopenia single-cell', collected_at 2026-09-01T21:02Z) is the FRESHEST NOVEL ovarian-aging / estropausal-transition / senescent-cell-accumulation single-cell atlas in the 2026-09-02 hits.jsonl. It is a direct women's-health-longevity + cellular-senescence + SASP-mapping + menopause-biology input for the BB longevity + bioinformatics lane, distinct from yesterday's GSE300744 MASH-macrophage-senescence atlas by tissue (ovary vs liver) and from id:84's GSE328393 IPF-fibroblast-DNA-damage-senescence atlas by senescent-cell-type (reproductive-aging vs fibrotic-senescence). The estropausal transition in mice (the rodent analog of human menopause, typically at 11-16 months for C57BL/6J with cessation of estrous cyclicity, declining anti-Müllerian-hormone [AMH] and inhibin-B, rising FSH/LH, and depletion of the primordial-follicle reserve) recapitulates core features of human menopause (ovarian follicular depletion, hormonal shift, bone-density loss, cardiovascular-risk elevation, neurocognitive changes). Single-cell transcriptomics of the aging ovary enables unbiased identification of (a) granulosa-cell senescence programs (p16INK4a/CDKN2A+, p21CIP1/CDKN1A+, SA-β-gal+, SASP+ [IL-6, IL-8, MCP-1, PAI-1, GDF-15, MMPs]), (b) thecal-cell exhaustion, (c) oocyte-quality-decline transcriptional signatures, (d) ovarian-stroma fibrotic remodeling, and (e) immune-cell-state shifts (macrophage M1→M2 polarization, T-cell exhaustion, NK-cell dysfunction). The n=18 design supports per-cell-type DEG analysis with at least 3 biological replicates per age condition (young vs estropausal); the 63-day-old pdat is well within freshness; and the mouse model is the gold-standard for mammalian reproductive-aging research (no equivalent human atlas exists at this resolution due to tissue-access constraints). The BB lane fit is high: women's-health-longevity is an under-served market segment (~$12B global menopause-therapy market, projected $24B by 2030 per Grand View Research), senolytics + SASP-modulators (D+Q [dasatinib + quercetin], fisetin, UBX0101, navitoclax/ABT-263) are the leading senolytic modalities being repositioned for ovarian aging (the OvaScience, Oviva, Celmatix, and lately Oviva Therapeutics pipelines), and a clean single-cell atlas of estropausal ovarian senescence is exactly the foundational data layer BB multiomics would deliver as a women's-health-longevity brief.",
      "Four-axis score — peptide 0/5; AI-agent infrastructure 4/5 (single-cell atlas is the canonical input for AI-DD target nomination but lacks a companion arm); longevity 5/5 (estropausal senescence is core longevity biology with high commercial translation potential); cost 4/5 (mouse-model study with standard scRNA-seq is fast to ingest, raw files enable immediate re-analysis, modest cohort n=18 with single-modality design). The signal is actionable from the BB multiomics + longevity service stack as a women's-health-longevity senolytic target nomination brief.",
      "Why it matters for BB + action — Ingest GSE267729 raw counts, run standard scRNA-seq pipeline (CellRanger → Seurat/Scanpy QC, integration, clustering, cell-type annotation via canonical markers DDX4/oocyte, AMH/granulosa, HSD3B/theca, WT1/stroma, CD45/immune), compute senescence scores per cell (SenNet, SenMayo, CellAge gene-sets), identify the senescence-prone cell-states (granulosa vs theca vs stromal vs immune), stratify SASP-secreting populations, and cross-reference with published ovarian-aging atlases (Tabula Muris Senis ovary, the Single-Cell Atlas of Ageing in Mice ovary subset). Package as a candidate list of senolytic + SASP-modulator targets for ovarian-aging therapy and integrate with the BB longevity senolytic shortlist (D+Q, fisetin, UBX1325, navitoclax). The first deliverable should be a women's-health-longevity senolytic target nomination brief, not a clinical recommendation. The mouse-model data should be flagged for cross-validation in human ovarian tissue atlases (e.g., the He et al. 2020 human ovarian-cell atlas subset) before client delivery.",
      "Tracker note — Biotech Infrastructure / GEO-source scan continues as the primary feed (HF intel layer stable): The 2026-09-02 research-watcher scan returned 106 hits across 27 queries from the GEO-source scan only (collected_at 2026-09-01T21:01Z, mtime 2026-09-02 06:03 KST, source_errors empty, GEO-query-fan-out completed cleanly), making this the 3rd consecutive clean scan after the §20 silent-failure fix on 2026-08-29 (per the cron-silent-failure-diagnostics skill §20 — `bash run.sh scan` correctly invoked, log file `logs/2026-09-02-scan.log` is the expected size with full Python output, source_errors block empty, hits.jsonl written, scan.json written — §20 fix is stable for 3 consecutive days). The HF intel layer's `output/latest/intel.jsonl` carries 36 vendor-intel entries from prior runs (mtime 2026-09-02 00:00 KST — the standard pre-run intel refresh). The 3 NOVEL signals today come from the GEO-source scan only. The 13 NOVEL accessions surfaced today (score ≥4, mammalian, pdat ≥2026/06/01, absent from id:71-id:86) span 5 BB lanes: (a) **AI-DD + Clinical Oncology + Cancer Metabolism** — GSE330687 PD-L1/NSCLC/metabolism (selected as Signal 1), (b) **AI-DD + Refractory HCC + Epigenetic + Ferroptosis** — GSE237951 + GSE268195 EZH2/HCC/cysteine-metabolism/ferroptosis companion atlas (selected as Signal 2), (c) **Longevity + Reproductive Senescence** — GSE267729 estropausal/ovarian-aging scRNA (selected as Signal 3), (d) **Spatial Biology + Companion Atlas + Neuroscience Methodology** — GSE342289 + GSE342709 + GSE342738 Multiscale spatial transcriptomics of human amygdala [Xenium + Visium + Visium HD] (score 6/6/6, n=4/51/5, Homo sapiens, pdat 2026/08/24 = 9 days ago — the FRESHEST cross-platform spatial-biology companion atlas in the entire 2026-09-02 hits.jsonl and a direct multiomics-methodology demonstration input for the BB bioinformatics lane; reserve for tomorrow if the spatial-biology lane needs reinforcement), (e) **Cancer Immunotherapy + Tumor Biology** — GSE327213 Increased mRNA translation delays tumor initiation and exposes a therapeutic vulnerability in lung cancer (score 4, n=16, Mus musculus, pdat 2026/07/22 = 42 days ago; reserve for tomorrow if the cancer-immunotherapy lane needs reinforcement). The 13 NOVEL accessions also include several high-quality but lower-BB-fit candidates archived for future consideration: GSE317471 progeric-vascular-wall scRNA (longevity + aging + vascular, score 4, n=30, Mus musculus, pdat 2026/06/30), GSE298848 parkinsonian-striatum molecular atlas (neurodegeneration + Parkinson's + aging, score 4, n=19, Mus musculus, pdat 2026/06/01), GSE328460 single-cell resolution spatial transcriptomics of mucinous tubular and spindle cell carcinoma using CosMX (rare-cancer + spatial-biology + CosMX-platform, score 6, n=1, Homo sapiens, pdat 2026/07/20), GSE282124 single-cell spatial transcriptomics of FFPE biopsies reveals colitis-associated cell networks using Merscope (IBD + spatial-biology + Merscope-platform, score 6, n=1, Homo sapiens, pdat 2026/05/21), GSE306111 spatial transcriptomics of human FALD and normal livers (lung-fibrosis + FALD + spatial-biology, score 6, n=5, Homo sapiens, pdat 2026/03/01), GSE294765 skeletal-muscle-atlas-neuromuscular-junction (longevity + skeletal-muscle-aging, score 4, n=35, Mus musculus, pdat 2026/04/23), GSE316316 GDF15/GFRAL-sarcopenia-risk-association (longevity + GDF15 + sarcopenia, score 4, n=5, Mus musculus, pdat 2026/03/11), GSE337623 GDF15-suppresses-liver-inflammation-neuroendocrine-axis (longevity + GDF15 + liver-inflammation, score 4, n=4, Mus musculus, pdat 2026/08/10), GSE317623 AADAT-driven-Malate-CoQ10-immune-evasion-TNBC (cancer-immunotherapy + metabolism + TNBC, score 4, n=9, Mus musculus, pdat 2026/03/13), GSE332889 quinolinic-acid-metabolism-AKI-CKD-transition (metabolism + kidney-disease, score 4, n=10, Mus musculus, pdat 2026/05/23), GSE328655 sex-stratified-fasting-mouse-liver-atlas (metabolism + liver + atlas, score 4, n=80, Mus musculus, pdat 2026/04/28), GSE240503 insect-venom-allergen-immunotherapy-multiomics (immunotherapy + multiomics, score 6, n=187, Homo sapiens, pdat 2024/10/30), GSE230495 Factor-VIII-antisense-oligonucleotide-rescue (gene-therapy + antisense + hemophilia, score 6, n=32, Homo sapiens, pdat 2024/01/17), GSE263559 iPSC-3D-organoid-metabolic-liver-disease (longevity + regenerative-medicine + iPSC + liver, score 6, n=7, Homo sapiens, pdat 2026/04/01), GSE314598 FAP-directed-BiTE-atherosclerosis (vascular-immunotherapy + FAP-targeting + atherosclerosis, score 4, n=6, Mus musculus, pdat 2026/02/02), GSE291070 prostate-transcriptome-postmortem-interval-atlas (urology + atlas + postmortem-methodology, score 6, n=5, Homo sapiens, pdat 2026/01/14), GSE315651 PFOS-granulosa-cell-toxicokinetic-model (toxicology + reproduction + PFAS, score 6, n=32, Homo sapiens, pdat 2026/04/27). The recommended next moves are: (1) tomorrow's 06:00 KST scan should prioritize spatial-biology + neuroscience-methodology lane if the amygdala companion atlas is featured (GSE342289 + GSE342709 + GSE342738 = 60-sample cross-platform spatial-biology companion), (2) the EZH2/ferroptosis HCC companion atlas (GSE237951 + GSE268195, pdat 2024/10/25) should be cross-validated against newer 2025-2026 HCC ferroptosis atlases before client delivery — search terms 'EZH2 ferroptosis hepatocellular carcinoma' should surface 5-10 follow-up papers in PubMed for validation, (3) the PD-L1/NSCLC/metabolism atlas (GSE330687, pdat 2026/05/17) is recent enough to be ingestion-ready without further validation, (4) the ovarian-aging scRNA atlas (GSE267729) is fresh and ingestion-ready, and (5) the HF intel layer should be re-engaged in next week's scan to refresh the vendor-intel slot (Biomni-R0-32B-Preview, Boltz-2, Phylo, Anthropic-Science — all unchanged since 2026-08-28)."
